   1.3 Process of Betterment in Model:
       1.3.1 Train and Test (80:20 or 70:30)
             ---> It avoids OverFitting and UnderFitting
       1.3.2 Estimate the Model by its metrics
             1.3.2.1 Regression
                     r2_score, mean_squared_error, absolute_mean_error
             1.3.2.2 Classification
                     accuracy_score, precision, recall, confusion_matrix, classification_report
       1.3.3 Cross Validate the input - cross-validation
             1.3.3.1 KFold (CV = 5) - Ensure training and testing done on all layer of datas
             1.3.3.2 StratifiedKFold(CV = 5) -  Ensure to train and test with exact category count
                     100 Rows ---> 70%True 30%False
                     Fold 1  - 70train(True,False) - 30test
                     Fold 2
                     Fold 3
                     Fold 4
                     Fold 5
       1.3.4 HyperparameterTuning - fit and predict using certain parameter is called

              model = RandomForestClassifier() #model without parameter (Default)
              model.fit(x_train, y_train)
              prediction = model.predict(x_test)

              model = RandomForestClassifier(criterion="entropy") #model with specific parameter
              model.fit(x_train, y_train)
              prediction = model.predict(x_test)

              grid_parameter = {"criterion":["gini","entropy"],
                            "max_depth":[0,2,4,6,8],
                            "min_samples_split:[None, 2, 5]}
              model = RandomForestClassifier()
              grid_search = GridSearchCV(model, grid_search=grid_parameter,x, y, cv=5, metric="accuracy")
              grid_search.fit(x, y)
              best_estimator = grid_search.best_estimators_
              prediction = best_estimator.predict(x_test)

   1.4 Model Choosing Criteria:
          1.4.1 Output (target - dependent data - y data)
               1.4.1.1 Regression
                      When output stays in Continuous value
               1.4.1.2 Classification
                      When output stays in Categorical Data
                      Types of Classification:
                      a. Binary (True or False, 1 or 0 , yes or no)
                      b. MultiClassifier (Load iris - setosa, virginca, versicolor)

          1.4.2 Input  (Feature - independent data - x data)
                Types:
                        a Numbers(int, float)
                        b Categories(str - object)
                1.4.2.1 Linear vs Non-Linear
                      Linear --> when one column is having linear over the other data
                      Non-Linear --> When one column doest have relationship over the other data
                1.4.2.2 parametric vs Non-Parametric
                      Parametric --> Relationship over the columns
                      Non-Parametric --> Relationship over rows and columns
                1.4.2.3 Distribution Based
                       Normally Distributed
                       Uniformally Distributed
   1.5 Models
     1.5.1 Supervised - Knowing what is our target or label
        1. LinearRegression
        2. LogisticRegression
        3. DecisionTree(DecisionTreeRegressor and DecisionTreeClassifier)
            model = DecisionTreeClassifier()
        4. RandomForest(RandomForestRegressor and RandomForestClassifier)
